+    To also alert when a mount's usage unexpectedly drops below some floor
+    (for example because the filesystem failed to mount and the mount point
+    is just an empty directory on the root filesystem), pass a mapping with
+    ``min`` and/or ``max`` keys instead of a single value. ``max`` behaves
+    exactly like the plain percentage above; ``min`` emits a beacon when
+    usage falls below the given percentage. Either key may be omitted.
